Modifications from upstream
---------------------------

Three regular expressions were changed to fix a portability defect. Upstream
writes Unicode ranges as `\u{E0000}`, which is JavaScript/Rust regex syntax.
Python's `re` module accepts only `\uXXXX` / `\UXXXXXXXX`, so `re.compile`
raised `re.PatternError` and `PromptThreatDetector()` could not be constructed
at all. The affected patterns are the "Unicode标签混淆" signature,
`_detect_zero_width_payload`, and the ASCII-smuggling check in
`_detect_markdown_exfil`.

The escapes were rewritten to the equivalent Python form (`\u{E0000}` ->
`\U000E0000`). No keyword, weight, threshold, or detection semantic was
altered; the character ranges match upstream's intent exactly.

No other change was made to the rule data.

